{:edb/db-before-t 1960 :edb/db-after-t 1961 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535273 50 #inst "2026-10-08T21:00:15.208Z" 13194139535273 true] [17592186172018 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341096 13194139535273 true] [17592186172018 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341117 13194139535273 true] [17592186172019 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341103 13194139535273 true] [17592186172019 1020 #edb/ref 17592186341110 13194139535273 true] [17592186172212 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535273 true] [17592186172212 1100 "Determine the domain of the vector field $F$ on $R^{2}$, given by\n\n$\\mathbf{F} ( x , y ) = \\frac{y}{{x}^{2} + {y}^{2}} \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\frac{x}{{x}^{2} - {y}^{2}} \\, \\mathbf{j} \\, .$." 13194139535273 false] [17592186172212 1100 "Determine the domain of the vector field $F$ on ${R}^{2},$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}\\,j\\,.\n$$" 13194139535273 true] [17592186172212 1145 "The function $F$ can be expressed in terms of its components $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)$ as\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},\\,Q(x,y)=\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe first find the domain of each component function. Then, we compute their intersection to find the domain of $F:$\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is defined everywhere other than when the denominator vanishes. To find where the denominator vanishes, we set it equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=0\\,⟹\\,x=y=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $P$ is given by\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,(x,y)\\ne (0,0)}.\n$$\n\n- The function $Q(x,y)$ is defined everywhere other than when the denominator vanishes. To find where the denominator vanishes, we set it equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=0\\,⟹\\,y=\\pm x\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $Q$ is given by\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y\\ne \\pm x}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the domain $D$ of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={D}_{1}\\cap {D}_{2}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,y\\ne \\pm x}\\,.\n$$" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341096 1017 #edb/ref 17592186341097 13194139535273 true] [17592186341096 1089 "q-122660" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341096 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535273 true] [17592186341096 1100 "Determine the domain of the vector field $F$ on ${R}^{2},$ given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4})\\,i+\\frac{xy}{x-1}\\,j\\,.\n$$" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341096 1113 #uuid "76ab55a5-b7ae-513b-bef2-54d7a5d78561" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341096 1145 "The function $F$ can be expressed in terms of its components $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)$ as\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4}),\\,Q(x,y)=\\frac{xy}{x-1}.\n$$\n\nWe first find the domain of each component function. Then, we compute their intersection to find the domain of $F:$\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is defined everywhere other than when the denominator vanishes. To find where the denominator vanishes, we set it equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-4=0\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $P$ is given by\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4}.\n$$\n\n- The function $Q(x,y)$ is defined everywhere other than when the denominator vanishes. To find where the denominator vanishes, we set it equal to zero and solve:\n\n$$\nx-1=0\\,⟹\\,x=1\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $Q$ is given by\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x\\ne 1}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the domain $D$ of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={D}_{1}\\cap {D}_{2}={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4,\\,x\\ne 1}\\,.\n$$" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341097 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341098 13194139535273 true] [17592186341097 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341099 13194139535273 true] [17592186341097 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341100 13194139535273 true] [17592186341097 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341101 13194139535273 true] [17592186341097 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341102 13194139535273 true] [17592186341097 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535273 true] [17592186341097 1041 "selection" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341097 1104 #edb/ref 17592186341100 13194139535273 true] [17592186341097 1110 #uuid "72dd5def-6976-59bc-873c-3d8ebef8e768" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341098 1034 "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,x\\ne 1}" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341098 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535273 true] [17592186341098 1111 #uuid "ed746dc3-9f51-59f0-aead-0b4738bf53b6" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341099 1034 "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4}" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341099 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535273 true] [17592186341099 1111 #uuid "382a6ac4-4b0c-548d-ade1-b2566d6843b5" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341100 1034 "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 4,\\,x\\ne 1}" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341100 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535273 true] [17592186341100 1111 #uuid "4b6aca0e-c557-5f15-aa31-343047fba81f" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341101 1034 "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4}" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341101 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535273 true] [17592186341101 1111 #uuid "e8036336-f315-5293-b75b-8fb505c40d85" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341102 1034 "{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>4}" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341102 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535273 true] [17592186341102 1111 #uuid "13395398-ea67-55a6-a2fe-9a5f8f74f59e" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341103 1017 #edb/ref 17592186341104 13194139535273 true] [17592186341103 1089 "q-122685" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341103 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535273 true] [17592186341103 1100 "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\n- $T(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,j+{z}^{2}\\,k$\n- $U(t)=2t\\,i-{t}^{2}\\,j-\\sqrt{t}\\,k$\n- $V(x,y,z)={e}^{-2z}\\sqrt{x+y}$" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341103 1113 #uuid "086063e9-05eb-5d55-a741-bf5ec8233d7b" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341103 1145 "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $T(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point $(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}$ to a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $U(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $V(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{3}$ to functions in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341105 13194139535273 true] [17592186341104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341106 13194139535273 true] [17592186341104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341107 13194139535273 true] [17592186341104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341108 13194139535273 true] [17592186341104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341109 13194139535273 true] [17592186341104 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535273 true] [17592186341104 1041 "selection" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341104 1104 #edb/ref 17592186341106 13194139535273 true] [17592186341104 1110 #uuid "84ff913a-8f18-55e8-bafd-bb9c42d01c1c" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341105 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341105 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535273 true] [17592186341105 1111 #uuid "96e8fbc6-2055-580e-971b-59c91acb8375" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341106 1034 "I only" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341106 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535273 true] [17592186341106 1111 #uuid "a08b5f42-d6f8-51a1-a1c9-7d63d7fcbafd" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341107 1034 "III only" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341107 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535273 true] [17592186341107 1111 #uuid "c9e35abc-3303-56bd-88a9-5caf5d89a794" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341108 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341108 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535273 true] [17592186341108 1111 #uuid "d948be7d-56a0-5268-9c7b-1b3dc5eb032a" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341109 1034 "II only" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341109 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535273 true] [17592186341109 1111 #uuid "3cdbaf85-3d8b-522f-a03c-d8c7458ce51c" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341110 1017 #edb/ref 17592186341111 13194139535273 true] [17592186341110 1089 "q-122691" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341110 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535273 true] [17592186341110 1100 "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\n- $U(x,y,z)=(x+2){e}^{yz}$\n- $V(x,y,z)=⟨5{e}^{-{z}^{2}},{x}^{3}y,1-{y}^{3}⟩$\n- $W(x,y)=⟨x-3{y}^{2},2-y⟩$" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341110 1113 #uuid "c6a5608a-0fba-5a52-ac34-08b868b05a8a" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341110 1145 "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $U(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{3}$ to functions in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $V(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point $(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}$ to a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $W(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341112 13194139535273 true] [17592186341111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341113 13194139535273 true] [17592186341111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341114 13194139535273 true] [17592186341111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341115 13194139535273 true] [17592186341111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341116 13194139535273 true] [17592186341111 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535273 true] [1759218