domain of each component function. Then, we compute their intersection to find the domain of $F:$\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is defined when the expression under the logarithm is positive. So, to find the domain, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n1-{x}^{2}>0\\,⟹\\,-1<x<1.\n$$\n\nThis defines the region ${D}_{1},$ shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061075/assets/89c78ec587826c15c90ef4ffdfc0fd9f8af3d7b4d3d1cc099ce24b883b9842c2.png)\n\n- The function $Q(x,y)$ is defined the expression under the radical is positive or equal to zero. So, to find the domain, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n1-|y|\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,-1\\le y\\le 1.\n$$\n\nThis defines the region ${D}_{2},$ shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061075/assets/addd649aa739711fd34ebd3e82579c8c0100a2b9a109d5cafabde750bc94eb9a.png)\n\nFinally, the domain $D$ of $F$ is given by ${D}_{1}\\cap {D}_{2},$ shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061075/assets/49000dd6905017bc64c9a67b6d8a2ea475a684477ac6e02d6ed15c4c7dbbb3aa.png)" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341119 13194139535273 true] [17592186341118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341120 13194139535273 true] [17592186341118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341121 13194139535273 true] [17592186341118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341122 13194139535273 true] [17592186341118 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341123 13194139535273 true] [17592186341118 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535273 true] [17592186341118 1041 "selection" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341118 1104 #edb/ref 17592186341121 13194139535273 true] [17592186341118 1110 #uuid "13614c47-5b79-5bee-9be8-d11672cb5627" 13194139535273 true] [17592186341119 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14061075/as